== 0. Derivation (validate/linked_source_theory.jl; validate/symbolic/check_linked_source.jl, 51 checks PASS) ==

Exact: K_s = κ(B_s,B,l,l) = H_s − 2y_sY_l with H_s = Cov(B_sB, d_l²) (variance heterogeneity);
H_s = H2_s (Σ_{k∈s} Cov(d_k², d_l²)) + H3_s (three-locus); y_sY_l = Σ_k D_kl² + cross-pair products;
so K = two-locus cumulants (H2 − 2ΣD²) + three-locus cumulants. Biallelic l: d_l² − v_l = s_l d_l
(s_l = κ3_l/v_l), H_s = s_l κ(B_s,B,l), T_s = s_l y_s (spectrum shape).
Drift (iid sampling of M, exact to O(1/M²)): E[Ĥ] = (1 − 5/M)H + 4yY/M (exactly
(M−1)(M−2)[(M−2)H + 4yY]/M³), E[ŷŶ] = (1 − 3/M)yY + (H + Cov(B_s,B)v)/M,
E[K̂] = (1 − 7/M)K − (2/M)(Cov(B_s,B)v + 2yY): for biallelic loci exactly Ohta & Kimura's (1969) /
Hill & Robertson's (1968) E[D(1−2p)(1−2q)] and E[D²] equations. So H is seeded by drift only at
O(1/M) relative to yY, decays at 5/M + ρ, and its neutral pair fixed point is H/(2y²) = 2ε/(5ε+ρ) ≤ 0.4.
Survival subset: iid with 1/m − 1/M (leading order; exact enumeration). Single crossover: H ← p₀H
(p₀ = no split among k, j, l). Mutation: E[ΔH] = 0 exactly. Selection: dH/dε = κ₅(A,B,X,X,h) +
2[κ(A,X,h)Y + y_Aκ(B,X,h)] exactly; biallelic Δs = −2β(v + Y).

== 1. Decomposition of K on D (re-run of linked_decay's D runs, same seeds, extended instrumentation; 39 runs, 2902 thread-s) ==

Hypotheses before looking: (i) H is mostly two-locus (H2) from tightly linked pairs, seeded by drift
(O–K); (ii) the biallelic projection s_lJ explains most of H; (iii) the selection change of H per
generation is small next to the drift seed 4yY/(2n); (iv) H grows under the move through
selection on H.

