Reading (development):
 - The closure's gap is H: H/(2yY) = 0.41 before the move, 0.36–0.48 in 25..99, 0.62 in 100..199.
 - (i) partly false: the pairwise part is large but the three-locus part cancels much of it.
   Σ D_kl² ≈ 2 yY (the cross-pair LD products are ≈ −ΣD²); the two-locus cumulants are ≈ 3K and
   the three-locus cumulants ≈ −2K. H2 > H (H3 < 0), and under the move H2 grows 2–8× while H3
   turns more negative, so the net H changes much less than its parts.
 - (ii) holds: s_l J explains 0.63–0.91 of H and s_l Σκ(k,k,l) 0.79–0.93 of H2; s_l y explains
   0.75–0.93 of T. The residual within-locus variance of d² not explained by a biallelic locus is
   16–38% per input. So the variance heterogeneity is mostly skew × three-way LD, the spectrum's
   shape acting through the sign of a(1−2p).
 - (iii) false: the selection change of H is 20–70× the drift seed before the move (stabilising
   selection), positive. The selection change of the cumulant K is, before the move, a decay at
   1.7–2.6 × Var(G_chr)/S_c × (K + K3) per generation (≈ 2: the Leonov–Shiryaev terms
   c_B κ(B_s,l,l,G) + c_s κ(B,l,l,G), c = Cov(·, G_chr)), consistently over the 12 inputs with
   Var(G_chr)/S_c ≥ 0.008. K3 is small (|K3/K| ≤ 0.3 in 10 of 13). The LD-product candidates for
   ΔH (2β[(T+J)Y + y(C+J)], and the moment form) explain ≤ 0.2 of it: the fifth-order terms
   dominate. Under the move the ratios scatter (directional βκ₅ enters).
 - So K/(−2yY) < 1 before the move is a Bulmer effect on the fourth cumulant (it is pulled to zero
   at ≈ 2Var(G_chr)/S_c per generation, the LD's product at a slower rate), with the O(1/M) drift
   seeding of H (O–K) on top; F's weaker selection (larger ω) fits its ratio nearer 1 (0.86).

== 2. Closure (development on D) ==

Minimal extension kept (level B′): per class pair (s,t) the coupled (P, H) moments with the exact
O(1/M) drift terms at both sampling stages and the three-locus split probability, and the leading
stabilising-selection decay of the cumulant, K_st ← K_st − (c_s K_t· + c_t K_s·)/S_c. Dropped (and
why): directional βκ₅ (fifth order, not closable at this order; it is what makes the measured K fall
in 100..199), κ₆, K3 (small), products of third-order cumulants, 2v_lκ(B_s,B,l,G) (v_l ≪ Var(B)).
The T recursion's decay is unchanged.
Comparator: B′ drift-only (no selection term on K).

Hypothesis before the D comparison: B′ brings predicted K to within 25% of measured before the
move and in 50..99, and fixes level B's overprediction of ΣC in 25..99.

